url: "https://github.com/Nizoka/pkinative-mcp"
abstract: >-
  Model Context Protocol (MCP) server bridging the zero-dependency pkinative
  PKI engine to AI clients. Provides 34 tools for inspecting and verifying
  X.509 certificates, certification requests, CRLs, OCSP responses, CMS
  SignedData messages and RFC 3161 time-stamps; building and validating
  certificate chains (RFC 5280 path validation, RFC 6125 name checks,
  extended key usage, offline CRL and OCSP revocation); creating certificates,
  certification requests, CMS signatures, OCSP requests and time-stamp
  requests with keys that never leave the host's Web Crypto; opening PKCS#8
  keys and PKCS#12 files without returning a key byte; decoding and encoding
  ASN.1, PEM and object identifiers; an offline capability preflight, a code
  explainer and human-in-the-loop governance issue drafting. Every artefact
  the server writes is validated against OpenSSL 3 in continuous
  integration. Speaks MCP 2026-07-28 with automatic fallback for 2024- and
  2025-era clients and makes no network call, ever.
license: MIT
